ters. JS doesn't support named groups as far as I can tell, so we probably need a mapping structure between group index and parameter name, which might even obviate the need for the serializer function.\n\nThis could look like this:\n\n   {\n    name : 'Test',\n    regex: '^test/(.+)/(.+)$',\n    regex_group_names: ['a', 'b'],\n    serializer: (params) => {\n      return new GeneratedUrl(`test/${params.a}/${params.b}`, {});\n    },\n\nThen we should be able to always only populate a and b in the router params.\n\nFor more complex regex, and when no group names are given, we could still pass the match indexes to the component, if there is an advantageous case for that somehow - maybe in the case of dynamic number of groups?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/198445147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bastih","id":9842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih","html_url":"https://github.com/bastih","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bastih/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"actor":{"login":"bastih","id":9842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4ND